			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Complete service migration from Source/Effect/ to Source/Service/Effect/, prune dead Configuration module\n\nMove all 30+ Wind service domains from the outdated `Source/Effect/` path to the canonical `Source/Service/Effect/` hierarchy, updating barrel exports and JSDoc import paths accordingly. Delete the orphaned Configuration module — all 6 files under `Source/Effect/Configuration/` (ConfigApplyError, ConfigFetchError, ConfigValidationError, ConfigurationHelper, ConfigurationImplementation, ConfigurationService, ConfigurationMock, ConfigurationSchemaType, and index) — which became dead code when its functionality was absorbed into Bootstrap stages.\n\nActivate the deep-shim system at bootstrap time: wire EventInterceptor, NetworkProxy, and AsyncProxy into `TauriMainProcessService` constructor under the TierShim gate, ensuring DOM event interception, network routing, and async scheduling interception are installed before any workbench code executes. Add `createInterceptedInvoke` wrapper to both `_InvokeViaNode` and `InvokeMountain` so all MountainIPCInvoke calls flow through the IPCInterceptor for ShinkLevel-aware routing.\n\nReformat the entire codebase for consistent blank-line spacing between statement blocks, satisfying the format-pipeline blank-line formatter. Fix import ordering in shim modules (IPCInterceptor, EventInterceptor, Index) to match project convention. Improve type safety in AsyncProxy by replacing `@ts-nocheck` with proper typed originals and eliminating the nullable Originals pattern. Remove stale `effect` and `@effect/language-service` dependencies from package.json.\n\nImpact: Clean module boundaries under `Source/Service/Effect/`, zero dead Configuration code, and fully wired deep-shim activation at the Tauri service level. All 388 staged files pass formatting and type checks.",
			"SHA": "967049675678d7d31281e1af1983291819dbbc3f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:34:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				810,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add async scheduling and network proxy interceptors to deep-shim system\n\nIntroduce two new proxy layers for Land's deep-shim interception architecture, completing Layers E (network) and F (async scheduling) alongside the existing EventInterceptor (Layer D).\n\n**AsyncProxy (Source/Shim/AsyncProxy.ts):** Monkeys all 8 async scheduling primitives — setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval, requestAnimationFrame, cancelAnimationFrame, requestIdleCallback, cancelIdleCallback — routing zero-delay timers through a microtask batch flush for coalescing, tracking interval handles through an ActiveIntervals map for proper cleanup, and delegating rAF/rIC to Land's render/idle cycle. String-eval callbacks are safely wrapped.\n\n**NetworkProxy (Source/Shim/NetworkProxy.ts):** Intercepts global fetch() and XMLHttpRequest to route network calls through Land's service tree. Microsoft telemetry endpoints (dc.services.visualstudio.com, vortex.data.microsoft.com) are silently discarded with a 204 response. vscode-file:// URIs are routed to Mountain's scheme handler (501 stub pending wire-up). Extension gallery queries (marketplace.visualstudio.com, open-vsx.org) are forwarded to Land's GalleryService (501 stub pending wire-up). All other traffic passes through to the original fetch/XHR unchanged.\n\n**FullIndex (Source/Shim/FullIndex.ts):** Combined barrel export re-exporting the core shim (Index.ts) plus EventInterceptor, NetworkProxy, and AsyncProxy — the \"everything\" entry point for the deep-shim system. All exports are dead-code-eliminated by esbuild when TierShim=None.\n\n**Documentation:** Add Shim Compatibility section to Architecture.md with shim tier comparison table. Add a standalone Repository README.md with the same tier table pointing to the architecture doc.\n\nAll three new modules are gated behind the IsEnabled check from Gate.ts — zero runtime overhead when TierShim=None.",
			"SHA": "bfefeb33a21df23add80241edb7ef02836ee103a"
		}
